## Creating summary stats of the data

**summarise()** will collapse of the rows creating a single summary stat, it will delete not necessary columns


```{r, echo=TRUE}
gapminder %>%
  filter(year == 1967) %>%
  summarise(mean_gdpPerCapita = mean(gdpPercap))
```

## Most common summary stats

* Location: `mean()` and `median()`
* Dispersion: `sd()` and `IQR()`
* Rank: `min()`, `quantile(x, 0.25)` and `max()`
* Count: `n()` and `n_distinct()`

